--- CANDIDATE ANSWER ---
Yes—if the root command sets `TraverseChildren: true` (`command.go:225`). Execution then uses `c.Traverse(args)` (`command.go:1087-1091`), which collects flags and their values before locating the subcommand and parses them on the parent via `c.ParseFlags(flags)` (`command.go:793-824`).
